From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:41:57 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mesa/st: clip points and lines as GLES does in every context

This Mesa's GL contexts render only for virglrenderer, which runs every
guest on a desktop core context. A desktop context clips a point or
line against the whole clip volume: it drops a point whose vertex lies
outside and cuts a line at the volume's edges, so a wide one loses the
fragments it would put inside the viewport, while a wide one inside
spills past the viewport. A GLES guest expects only the near and far
planes to clip a point or line, and the viewport to bound every
fragment.
The virgl protocol does not carry the guest's API, so a GLES guest got
the desktop rule.

Upstream virglrenderer's host expectation lists record the result.
.gitlab-ci/expectations/host/virgl-gl-fails.txt, for a desktop GL host,
lists dEQP-GLES2 and dEQP-GLES3 clipping.point.wide_point_clip,
wide_point_clip_viewport_center and wide_point_clip_viewport_corner,
and clipping.line.wide_line_clip_viewport_center and
wide_line_clip_viewport_corner as failures. virgl-gles-fails.txt, for a
GLES host, lists none of them.

Vulkan clips the GLES way, so Zink already gives every guest that rule,
and lavapipe sets the flag itself. Set it for every context here too.
Only the drivers that clip in draw read it: llvmpipe and softpipe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_rasterizer.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_rasterizer.c b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_rasterizer.c
index 086a914b1649a0efde40ac14af87a1797b3c83d3..8c1f63794a75d194469127f5149ee8ffb6f5b1d8 100644
--- a/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_rasterizer.c
+++ b/src/mesa/state_tracker/st_atom_rasterizer.c
@@ -223,10 +223,14 @@ st_update_rasterizer(struct st_context *st)
       }
 
       raster->point_quad_rasterization = 1;
-
-      raster->point_line_tri_clip = _mesa_is_gles2(st->ctx);
    }
 
+   /* This Mesa renders only for virglrenderer, which runs every guest on a
+    * desktop context. Clip points and lines the way GLES and Vulkan do, as
+    * the devices' Vulkan drivers already do for every guest.
+    */
+   raster->point_line_tri_clip = 1;
+
    /* ST_NEW_VERTEX_PROGRAM
     */
    raster->point_size_per_vertex = st_point_size_per_vertex(ctx);
